# SfxLab family v2: layer id name type dur seed key=value... (dur 0 = endless) · range id param lo hi [note] · bind signal id|* param [lo hi] [rel] [steps=N | scale=<chord>] · note text · then `spell <id>` sections: name, recipe, the spell's layers at their lock values, its binds and notes
bench 1
root 65.4064
# aqueous: the notes are made by oscillators, the water recordings are accents. Each chord tone is a mellow tone through a resonant low-pass whose cutoff
# hops at random (sample-and-hold): the classic synth burble. The hopping slows to nothing as the ratios lock (still water) and its rate
# follows the pen's speed (flow). A wavering drone at C2 is the depth. The water recordings stay as accents: rumble, stream, droplets, splashes.
